# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""The English of APP 53/1455/0/2/21, page by page, and the summaries of its documents.

Written in session on 2026-10-21 from the Latin as read on the photographs
(text.py). A catchword is said once: the English of a page ends where the
copyist's last line ends, and the next page begins with the word he repeats.

Names. Christian names are given in their Polish form (Mikołaj, Jan, Piotr,
Kazimierz), as in the English of the edition's Kodeks Dyplomatyczny
Wielkopolski; surnames stand as written. Places the edition has settled are
given in its form (Ląd, Pyzdry, Konin, Kalisz, Zagórów, Łukom, Łukomia,
Drzewce, Imielno, Poznań, and Grądzyń for the copy's "Gradziem" and
"Gradzien": the editor, 2026-10-21); the rest stand as written (Makownica,
Malenin, Ruchocin, Lomowo, Lome and Lomy, Huta, Rosiszewo,
Tomice, Czernietz and its other spellings). "parvum Wronczyno" is Little
Wronczyn, as the edition's Kodeks English has Great Wronczyn for "Magnum
Wronczino" (the Kodeks: 1173 "parvum Vronchin", 1377 "Parvum Wronczino";
reference/places.yml, Wrąbczynek). A word read with doubt is
"[uncertain: ...]".

Terms: "mansus" is the mansus (łan), "Franconian mansi" the large measure
of the Frankish łan; "pertica" the rod; "scopulus" the boundary mound
(kopiec, the copyist's own gloss in 1362); "Ministerialis" the court
summoner (woźny); "Proconsul" the burgomaster; "advocatus" (in a town) the
wójt; "Palatinus" the voivode; "Subcamerarius" the sub-chamberlain
(podkomorzy); "Kmetho" the peasant (kmieć); "sep" and "naraz" (narzaz), the
levies in grain and livestock, and "powos" (powóz), the carting duty, stand
as the copyist names them.
"""

ENGLISH = {
 (1, '0013_a'): """Privilege of Mikołaj, heir, on the boundaries or limits of the village of Makownica. 14.

In the name of the Lord, Amen. For the perpetual memory of the matter. We, Mikołaj, heir of Venacia, general judge of the land of Kalisz, wish it to be known to all and each, present and to come, who will have knowledge of these presents: that, after mature deliberation and sound and sufficient counsel taken on it, desiring, with the help of the Almighty [uncertain: suffragio] first secured, to obtain a saving remedy for our soul and for the souls of our kin, and wishing our heritage, namely Makownica, which had earlier been resigned to our monastery of Ląd in the presence of the Most Serene Prince and Lord, Lord Władysław, by the grace of God illustrious King of Poland etc., and confirmed in perpetuity by his letters patent, to be more fully known and manifest in its bounds and boundaries, we ordered it, according to the custom of our land, a court summoner having been taken, to be marked with [uncertain: gadibus] or mounds, otherwise kopce in the vernacular, from the boundaries of the village of Malenin up to the boundaries of the heritage called Ruchocin, to dig them, in the vernacular [uncertain: odsuć], and to make the boundary: and so half of the thicket called Kobielnica, which flows or runs, Samica in the vernacular, shall belong in perpetuity to the said heritage of Makownica. We add besides to the foregoing, as a final disposition for a testament: that after our death the said monastery and the whole convent of its brothers of the Cistercian Order shall have, and shall possess peacefully for all time, the substance of all our goods contained there in the aforenamed heritage and [uncertain: postmo] to be contained there, namely the bees, cattle, sheep, mares, beasts, and generally all things, movable as well as immovable. In witness of which, lest it be annulled by those who come after, we have ordered these our letters to be written firmly and have strengthened them with the protection of our seal. Done at Ląd on the Sunday within the octave of Corpus Christi, in the same year 1399. Present: the discreet man Jakusz, parish priest at [uncertain: Czaten], and the noble men, the lords Jan [uncertain: Siemenci] Pech, castellan of Czarnków, Mikołaj [uncertain: Retch], burgrave of Pyzdry, [uncertain: Vito] Lukomski Jaszko of the same place, and very many others worthy of trust.""",

 (2, '0013_a'): """Privilege "Gradziem Ruchowia". 15.

In the name of the Lord, Amen. For the perpetual memory of the matter. We, Piotr of Szamotuły, castellan of Poznań, general captain of Greater Poland, make known by the tenor of these presents to all whom it concerns: that, coming to our knowledge and to the presence of other nobles of the same land, the honourable and noble lords Jan""",

 (2, '0014_a'): """Jan Wochneth, parish priest at Koscielec, Mikołaj Wochneth of Bartodzieje, and [uncertain: Barlyus] Wochneth of Osiecza, three brothers german, undivided; and also the honourable and noble Marcin Bochneth, Jan Bochneth and Maciej Bochneth, brothers german, heirs german of the aforesaid Jan Bochneth, parish priest at Koscielec, of Mikołaj of Bartodzieje and of [uncertain: Wardzch] of Osiecza, undivided in their said goods with their said paternal uncles; not compelled, not forced, nor led astray by any other error, but sound in mind and body, having used the wholesome counsel of their friends and having first deliberated maturely among themselves, resigned in perpetuity three whole mansi with gardens in the village and heritage of Łukom in the district of Konin, lying in the parish of Zagórów; the forest Grądzyń with the woods and groves and the Pyzdry mounds; with the forest Chmielniki and with the forest Lome, up to the road called Rosiszewska, which goes from Łukom and the village of Lomowo to the hill Karczemne gory, and the marshes otherwise called Karczemne Lugi; and with the field above Imielno; and with all right, dominion and property, as they alone held, had and possessed them, reserving for themselves and their lawful successors no right whatever of dominion or property in them; with all and singular plots, courts, houses, barns, fields, meadows, pastures, grasslands, forests, woods, groves, thickets, enclosures, brushwood, oak woods, scrub, pine woods, hills, rises, [uncertain: Stenis], marshes, lakes, ponds, peasants, labours, burdens, gardens and gardeners, and generally with all and singular useful fruits, incomes and revenues, by whatever name and word they are called, belonging and pertaining in any way to the said mansi and the other goods described and designated above, far and wide, as the said mansi are marked off and bounded round about in their bounds and limits; for four hundred marks of good broad middle groschen of the coin and count customary in Poland, reckoning forty-eight groschen to each mark; to the Reverend Father, Lord Cornelius, abbot, and the religious Jan, prior, and Wolmar, rector of the parish church at Ląd, and to the whole convent of the monastery of Ląd, having for this the consent and special will of the Most Serene Prince and Lord, Lord Kazimierz, by the grace of God King of Poland etc., our most gracious lord: for the said lords the abbot, the prior and the whole convent and their successors to hold, have and possess, to use and enjoy, to sell, alienate, exchange, give, donate, and turn to their own uses and pleasure, as shall seem better and more useful to them and their successors for the time being. In witness of which our seals are hung beneath these presents. Done and given at Pyzdry on the Monday next after the feast of the Exaltation of the Holy Cross, in the year 1461. Present there the well-born and noble lords Jan Swidwa the younger, Jan Sobocki, burgrave of Poznań, Mikołaj Kamski, [uncertain: Gavisso] Gorecki, Mikołaj Dabrowski, Krystyn Goszdychowski, and many others worthy of trust in the matters above.

[Written in the margin:]

And with the forest of Lomy, from the boundaries""",

 (3, '0014_a'): """Confirmation of Grądzyń by King Kazimierz. 16.

In the name of the Lord, Amen. For the perpetual memory of the matter. We, Kazimierz, by the grace of God King of Poland, and also of the lands of Kraków, Sandomierz, Sieradz, Łęczyca and Kuyavia, Grand Duke of Lithuania, lord and heir of Pomerania and Prussia etc., make known by the tenor of these presents to all whom it concerns, present and to come, who will have knowledge of them, how, coming to our presence and that of our prelates and barons""",

 (3, '0015_a'): """the venerable and religious Maciej, abbot of the monastery of Ląd, our devout and beloved, made known to us by his statement that he had made a contract of purchase with the noble Mikołaj, Jan and Warsz, brothers german of Koscielec, heirs, and with their stepson, for three mansi or łany of fields lying in the village of Łukomia in the district of Konin, and for the forest called Grądzyń, and also other forests and woods, meadows, fields, heaths, fishponds, beehives, waters and their courses, and all other profits, uses and revenues belonging in any way of old to the said three mansi or łany, as the heirs written above have possessed them until now, reserving to themselves and their successors no right of property or dominion in them; and humbly and devoutly besought our majesty with due instance that we might give our gracious consent and assent to the said contract of purchase. We, then, wishing to buy heavenly things for earthly ones and to enlarge divine worship in that venerable monastery of Ląd, and especially considering the lack of forests and woods, with which that monastery might be restored in its [uncertain: Casanis] and old ruins, since it lacks them elsewhere, namely forests and woods; and so that, for our happy arrival when we happen to come down there, the necessaries might be had the better: graciously inclined to the prayers of the said abbot, we have given our gracious will to the said contract of purchase of the said three łany, forests, woods and all other appurtenances, made, as is touched on above, by the abbot himself and his convent; we have assented, and by these presents assent, decreeing that it shall have the strength of perpetual validity. In witness of which our seal is hung on these presents. Done at Gniezno on the Tuesday before the feast of St Lawrence the Martyr, in the year of the Lord [uncertain: 1447]. Present: the Reverend Father, Lord Andrzej, bishop, and the magnificent and noble Łukasz of Górka, of Poznań, and Marcin of [uncertain: Rasko], of Kalisz, voivodes; [uncertain: Dobrogosto] of Szamotuły, of Poznań, Przedbor of Koniecpol, of Sandomierz, and Piotr of Kurów, of Sącz, castellans; and many other witnesses worthy of trust to the present. Given by the hands of the magnificent Jan of Koniecpol, chancellor, and Piotr of [uncertain: Tczenaczmy], vice-chancellor, our sincerely beloved.""",

 (4, '0025_a'): """Privilege, or exchange, of the village of Little Wronczyn and of the mill in the suburb of Pyzdry with Kazimierz, King of Poland, for the forest Czernietz, in which the village of Drzewce [uncertain: est] was afterwards founded. 25.

In the name of the Lord. Amen. Lest the affairs or deeds of mortals that are done and ordained in time pass away and waver with the course of time, it is necessary that they be brought to perpetual memory by the safeguard of letters and the noting of witnesses. Therefore let the present age, as well as the future, know: that we, Kazimierz, by the grace of God King of Poland, and also lord and heir of the lands of Kraków, Sandomierz, Sieradz, Łęczyca, Kuyavia, Pomerania and Ruthenia, after mature deliberation, and with the common counsel of our barons joining in it, have made an exchange of our royal goods, namely of the deserted forests described expressly below, with the venerable and religious man Brother Jan, abbot, and the convent of the brothers of the monastery of Ląd, of the Cistercian Order, of the Gniezno district, in this manner. The heritage of that monastery, namely Little Wronczyn near the town of Pyzdry, and the mill below the castle of Pyzdry, also of the said monastery of Ląd, with all and singular rents, fruits, profits and appurtenances belonging in any way of old to the said heritage of Wronczyn and the said mill, as they are marked off all round in their boundaries, being received, appropriated and incorporated in perpetuity for us and our kingdom by way and in the name of exchange: which heritage of Wronczyn with the mill above-said the lord abbot aforesaid, in his own name and that of his convent, by way of exchange, freely and willingly resigned from himself and his said monastery of Ląd to us and our kingdom, to hold and have in perpetuity, as he is permitted, with all right and dominion. In recompense for the said heritage and mill, we give, donate, ascribe and appropriate to the same lord abbot and his monastery and convent aforesaid, in the manner and by way of exchange, our forest in the part commonly called Czirnetz, situated in the district of Konin, fit for the cultivation of fields, containing sixty Franconian mansi in their due measure, measured by our authority and by our special messengers, and duly bounded and surrounded all round on every side, from all heritages, our royal ones as well as those of any nobles lying around, by its certain boundaries, which are commonly called kopce, with all profits and fruits whatever that are in that forest or may in any way be in it in future; and by the tenor of these presents, for all time, with all right and dominion, as it""",

 (4, '0026_a'): """belonged to us, we incorporate it under our protection, to be possessed for their benefit. We give the abbot and convent aforesaid full and complete power to found in the forest of the said sixty mansi as many villages as they can, under Polish or German law, as shall seem to them more useful and expedient. And we will that the villages founded in the said forest shall fully enjoy and possess, by our special grace, every freedom from our royal payments whatever which the other possessions of the said monastery of Ląd enjoy, as is more fully contained in the ancient privileges made on the freedom of the possessions of that monastery. But if the same abbot and convent should be unwilling or unable to settle these sixty mansi to the full, then in whatever part of them they leave as a grove or forest, the hunting of deer and boar being reserved in it for our royal pleasure, all other profits, fruits and revenues, namely in pastures, spaces, and the hunting of any wild beasts or birds, and also by name all and singular profits customarily had by us in the said forests, as they belonged to us and as we alone held them under our royal power: all the foregoing the abbot and convent of the above-said monastery of Ląd shall hold for all time, as from now ascribed and incorporated to them by us, and shall possess peacefully and quietly, with our special requisition made beforehand, to sell, give, exchange and turn them in any way to the use of themselves and their oft-said monastery of Ląd. In witness of which our seal is hung on these presents. Done at Pyzdry on the Tuesday after the octave of the Epiphany of the Lord, in the year of the same 1362. Present these witnesses: Albert, voivode of Brześć; Wyrzbięta, castellan of Poznań and captain of Poland; Janusz of [uncertain: Bechovien.] and Dobiesław of Kruszwica, castellans; Adam of Kalisz and Trojan of Brześć, sub-chamberlains; and Florian, chancellor of Łęczyca, by whose mandate the present privilege [uncertain: transmitti]; and very many other witnesses worthy of trust.""",

 (5, '0026_a'): """Privilege of freedom from Polish exactions for the colonists settled in Czernetz. 26.

Let all, present and to come, who will have knowledge of these presents, know: that we, Kazimierz, by the grace of God King of Poland, wishing to enlarge the profits of our kingdom further, and that the forest which we gave and granted by reason of an exchange to the religious men, the abbot and convent of the monastery at Ląd, of the Cistercian Order, should grow into richer fruit (in which forest, called in the vernacular Czernetz, lying in the land of Kalisz, the said abbot and convent of the monastery at Ląd are to have sixty mansi or łany, sufficiently and fully measured), and that the said sixty mansi might be settled more easily and diligently, or be possessed by any colonists, give and grant to all and every peasant or inhabitant who has been or shall be settled in the said forest Czerletz, or on the said mansi now belonging to the said monastery at Ląd, full and complete freedom for twenty continuous years from the date of these presents. We release the said peasants who have been settled on the said sixty mansi by the abbot or the monastery of Ląd in the said forest Czernetz from all exactions, namely sep, naraz, the pig, the cow, the sheep, powos, carting of any kind, and all other services and extra services by whatever name they are called; and in particular we will that no castellan or official""",

 (6, '0066_a'): """the eighth by an oak not far from the same road, at thirty-four rods; the ninth at fifty rods; the tenth by the road that runs from Huta to Grądzyń, at forty rods. Going on further by the forest of Lomy, crossing the same road, the eleventh at fifty rods; the twelfth likewise at fifty rods, opposite the tilled land; the road running from Huta to Rosiszewo having been crossed, the thirteenth at seventy rods; the fourteenth likewise at seventy rods, near the road stretching on the left-hand side from Huta to Lomowo. And so, crossing the road that runs from Drzewce and Lomowo to Grądzyń, the parties came to the road that runs from Łukom to Lomowo, called the Rosiszewo road, and by that same road, at eighty rods, the fifteenth was raised. And from that mound, turning to the west and south by that same road, and crossing the other road, going from Grądzyń to Drzewce, in a raised place, at forty-five rods, the sixteenth mound was heaped up. Then the parties came to the road that runs from Tomice to Zagórów and Łukom: at thirty rods the seventeenth; going along that same road between the south and the west, at eighty rods the eighteenth; and at twenty rods, by the same road, the nineteenth mound was raised. Further, then, taking the course of the road that runs to the corner mounds of the estates of Tomice and of the town of Pyzdry, the boundary is to be marked. The boundary wall of the estate of Łukomia with Grądzyń being thus dispatched, the compromissory court, at the parties' wish, went down to open two small hills towards Huta belonging to the estate of Łukom, near a muddy place, five paces apart from each other, in the earlier boundary marks, which the venerable convent of Ląd had taken for wall mounds; when they were opened nothing was found. At last, on the next day, namely the Friday next after the same Sunday Misericordia, the present compromissory court, pressing on at the parties' wish, betook itself to the renewal of the mounds between the estate of Łukom on the one part, the town of Zagórów on the other, and Drzewce on the third, and, its jurisdiction resumed through the court summoner written above, in the presence of those set down above [uncertain: attendentique], by virtue of the privileges graciously given to it by the Most Serene Kings of Poland, of the respectable and renowned Maciej Kwiecinski, burgomaster, Albert Rozewicz, wójt, Antoni Zalewski, notary, Jan Ogorkiewicz, Antoni Nowicki, Kazimierz [uncertain: Bylczynski], Antoni Jankowski, Filip Rudkowski, Kazimierz Bekanowski, Tomasz""",
}

S = {
 1: ('Abschrift (Nr. 14 des Kopialbuchs, aus dem 18. Jahrhundert) einer lateinischen Urkunde, gegeben in Ląd am Sonntag in der Oktav von Fronleichnam 1399 (1. Juni). Mikołaj, Erbherr von Venacia und Generalrichter des Landes Kalisch, lässt sein Gut Makownica, das er zuvor vor König Władysław dem Kloster Ląd aufgelassen hatte und das der König mit offenem Brief bestätigt hatte, nach dem Brauch des Landes mit einem Gerichtsboten durch Grenzhügel (kopce) abgrenzen, von den Grenzen des Dorfes Malenin bis zu denen des Erbguts Ruchocin; die Hälfte des Gebüschs Kobielnica soll für immer zu Makownica gehören. Dazu bestimmt er als letzten Willen, dass das Kloster und sein Konvent nach seinem Tod seine ganze Habe in Makownica erhalten: Bienen, Vieh, Schafe, Stuten und alle beweglichen und unbeweglichen Dinge. Zeugen sind der Pfarrer Jakusz, der Kastellan von Czarnków, der Burggraf von Pyzdry und andere.',
     'A copy (no. 14 of the eighteenth-century copy-book) of a Latin charter given at Ląd on the Sunday within the octave of Corpus Christi 1399 (1 June). Mikołaj, heir of Venacia and general judge of the land of Kalisz, has his estate of Makownica, which he had earlier resigned to the monastery of Ląd before King Władysław and which the king had confirmed by letters patent, marked out by boundary mounds (kopce) with a court summoner, by the custom of the land, from the boundaries of the village of Malenin to those of the heritage of Ruchocin; half of the thicket of Kobielnica is to belong to Makownica for ever. He adds, as his last will, that after his death the monastery and its convent are to have all his goods in Makownica: bees, cattle, sheep, mares and all things movable and immovable. The witnesses are the parish priest Jakusz, the castellan of Czarnków, the burgrave of Pyzdry and others.'),
 2: ('Abschrift (Nr. 15 des Kopialbuchs, überschrieben „Privilegium Gradziem Ruchowia“) einer lateinischen Urkunde, gegeben in Pyzdry am Montag nach Kreuzerhöhung 1461 (21. September). Piotr von Szamotuły, Kastellan von Posen und Generalstarost von Großpolen, bezeugt, dass die ungeteilten Brüder Jan Wochneth, Pfarrer in Koscielec, Mikołaj Wochneth von Bartodzieje und ein dritter Bruder von Osiecza, zusammen mit ihren Neffen Marcin, Jan und Maciej Bochneth, dem Abt Cornelius, dem Prior Jan, Wolmar, dem Rektor der Pfarrkirche in Ląd, und dem ganzen Konvent von Ląd mit Zustimmung König Kasimirs auf ewig aufgelassen haben: drei ganze Hufen mit Gärten im Dorf und Erbgut Łukom im Bezirk Konin, in der Pfarrei Zagórów, dazu den Wald Grądzyń mit seinen Gehölzen, die Wälder Chmielniki und Lome bis zu dem Weg namens Rosiszewska, der von Łukom und dem Dorf Lomowo zum Hügel Karczemne gory führt, die Sümpfe Karczemne Lugi und ein Feld oberhalb von Imielno, mit allen Rechten und Nutzungen, ohne sich etwas vorzubehalten. Der Preis sind 400 Mark breiter Groschen, 48 Groschen auf die Mark. Unter den Zeugen ist Jan Sobocki, Burggraf von Posen. Am Rand steht: „und mit dem Wald Lomy, von den Grenzen“.',
     'A copy (no. 15 of the copy-book, headed "Privilegium Gradziem Ruchowia") of a Latin charter given at Pyzdry on the Monday after the Exaltation of the Holy Cross 1461 (21 September). Piotr of Szamotuły, castellan of Poznań and general captain of Greater Poland, attests that the undivided brothers Jan Wochneth, parish priest at Koscielec, Mikołaj Wochneth of Bartodzieje and a third brother of Osiecza, together with their nephews Marcin, Jan and Maciej Bochneth, resigned for ever to Abbot Cornelius, Prior Jan, Wolmar, rector of the parish church at Ląd, and the whole convent of Ląd, with King Kazimierz\'s consent: three whole mansi with gardens in the village and heritage of Łukom in the district of Konin, in the parish of Zagórów, with the forest of Grądzyń and its woods, the forests of Chmielniki and Lome as far as the road called Rosiszewska, which runs from Łukom and the village of Lomowo to the hill of Karczemne gory, the marshes of Karczemne Lugi and a field above Imielno, with all rights and profits, reserving nothing to themselves. The price is 400 marks of broad groschen, 48 groschen to the mark. Among the witnesses is Jan Sobocki, burgrave of Poznań. In the margin is written "and with the forest of Lomy, from the boundaries".'),
 3: ('Abschrift (Nr. 16 des Kopialbuchs, überschrieben „Confirmatio Gradziem Regis Casimiri“, die Bestätigung von Grądzyń durch König Kasimir) einer lateinischen Urkunde König Kasimirs von Polen, gegeben in Gnesen am Dienstag vor dem Fest des heiligen Laurentius; das Jahr ist überschrieben und als 1447 gelesen, wie eine spätere Hand es am Rand vermerkt hat, und die genannten Zeugen hatten ihre Ämter in diesem Jahr inne (8. August 1447). Der Abt Maciej von Ląd hat dem König vorgetragen, er habe mit den Brüdern Mikołaj, Jan und Warsz von Koscielec, Erben, und ihrem Stiefsohn einen Kaufvertrag über drei Hufen Ackerland im Dorf Łukomia im Bezirk Konin und den Wald Grądzyń geschlossen, mit weiteren Wäldern, Wiesen, Feldern, Heiden, Fischteichen, Bienenstöcken und Gewässern, ohne dass die Verkäufer sich ein Recht daran vorbehielten, und hat um seine Zustimmung gebeten. Der König stimmt zu und bestätigt den Vertrag auf ewig: um Himmlisches für Irdisches zu erwerben und den Gottesdienst im Kloster zu mehren, vor allem aber, weil dem Kloster anderswo die Wälder fehlen, mit denen es wiederhergestellt werden könnte, und damit es bei seinen Besuchen dort besser versorgt sei. Unter den Zeugen sind der Bischof Andrzej, der Woiwode von Posen Łukasz von Górka und der Kastellan von Sandomierz Przedbor von Koniecpol; gegeben durch den Kanzler Jan von Koniecpol. Der Text beginnt am Fuß von S. 14 und endet auf S. 15, die unter seinem Ende abgeschnitten ist.',
     'A copy (no. 16 of the copy-book, headed "Confirmatio Gradziem Regis Casimiri", the confirmation of Grądzyń by King Kazimierz) of a Latin charter of King Kazimierz of Poland, given at Gniezno on the Tuesday before the feast of St Lawrence; the year is written over and read as 1447, as a later hand noted it in the margin, and the witnesses named held their offices in that year (8 August 1447). Abbot Maciej of Ląd has told the king that he made a contract of purchase with the brothers Mikołaj, Jan and Warsz of Koscielec, heirs, and their stepson, for three mansi of fields in the village of Łukomia in the district of Konin and the forest of Grądzyń, with further forests, meadows, fields, heaths, fishponds, beehives and waters, the sellers reserving no right in them, and has asked for his consent. The king consents and confirms the contract for ever: to buy heavenly things for earthly ones and to increase divine worship in the monastery, but above all because the monastery lacks forests elsewhere with which it might be restored, and so that it may be better provided when he visits. Among the witnesses are Bishop Andrzej, Łukasz of Górka, voivode of Poznań, and Przedbor of Koniecpol, castellan of Sandomierz; given by the chancellor, Jan of Koniecpol. The text begins at the foot of p. 14 and ends on p. 15, which is cut below its end.'),
 4: ('Abschrift (Nr. 25 des Kopialbuchs) einer lateinischen Urkunde König Kasimirs von Polen, gegeben in Pyzdry am Dienstag nach der Oktav von Epiphanias 1362 (18. Januar). Mit dem Rat seiner Barone tauscht der König mit Abt Jan und dem Konvent der Zisterzienser von Ląd: Das Kloster überlässt dem König und dem Reich sein Erbgut Klein-Wronczyn bei der Stadt Pyzdry und seine Mühle unter der Burg Pyzdry; dafür gibt der König dem Kloster auf ewig einen Teil seines Waldes, genannt Czirnetz, im Bezirk Konin, zur Rodung geeignet und sechzig fränkische Hufen groß, von seinen Boten vermessen und mit Grenzhügeln (kopce) umgrenzt. Das Kloster darf dort so viele Dörfer nach polnischem oder deutschem Recht anlegen, wie es will, und diese sollen von allen königlichen Abgaben so frei sein wie die übrigen Güter des Klosters. Was es als Wald stehen lässt, gehört ihm mit allen Nutzungen; nur die Jagd auf Hirsche und Wildschweine behält sich der König vor. Nach der Überschrift des Abschreibers wurde in diesem Wald später das Dorf Drzewce angelegt. Unter den Zeugen sind Albert, Woiwode von Brześć, Wyrzbięta, Kastellan von Posen, und Florian, Kanzler von Łęczyca.',
     'A copy (no. 25 of the copy-book) of a Latin charter of King Kazimierz of Poland, given at Pyzdry on the Tuesday after the octave of the Epiphany 1362 (18 January). With the counsel of his barons the king makes an exchange with Abbot Jan and the Cistercian convent of Ląd: the monastery gives the king and the kingdom its heritage of Little Wronczyn near the town of Pyzdry and its mill below the castle of Pyzdry; in return the king gives the monastery for ever a part of his forest called Czirnetz, in the district of Konin, fit for clearing and sixty Franconian mansi in size, measured by his messengers and bounded by boundary mounds (kopce). The monastery may found there as many villages as it wishes, under Polish or German law, and they are to be as free of all royal payments as the monastery\'s other estates. What it leaves as forest is its own with all profits; only the hunting of deer and boar the king keeps for himself. By the copyist\'s heading, the village of Drzewce was later founded in this forest. Among the witnesses are Albert, voivode of Brześć, Wyrzbięta, castellan of Poznań, and Florian, chancellor of Łęczyca.'),
 5: ('Der Anfang einer Abschrift (Nr. 26 des Kopialbuchs) eines Privilegs König Kasimirs von Polen für die Siedler im Wald Czernetz im Land Kalisch, den er dem Abt und Konvent von Ląd im Tausch gegeben hatte und in dem sie sechzig Hufen haben sollen (Dok. 4). Damit die Hufen leichter besiedelt werden, gewährt der König allen Bauern, die sich dort ansiedeln oder angesiedelt haben, zwanzig Jahre volle Freiheit vom Datum der Urkunde an und befreit sie von allen Abgaben und Diensten, die er aufzählt: sep, naraz, Schwein, Kuh, Schaf, powos und Fuhren aller Art. Der Text bricht am Ende von S. 26 ab, in dem Satz, mit dem der König will, dass kein Kastellan oder Amtmann …; der Rest und das Datum stehen auf S. 27, die nicht aufgenommen ist.',
     'The beginning of a copy (no. 26 of the copy-book) of a privilege of King Kazimierz of Poland for the settlers in the forest of Czernetz in the land of Kalisz, which he had given in exchange to the abbot and convent of Ląd and in which they are to have sixty mansi (doc. 4). So that the mansi may be settled more easily, the king grants all peasants who settle or have settled there twenty years of full freedom from the date of the charter, and releases them from all levies and services, which he lists: sep, naraz, the pig, the cow, the sheep, powos and carting of every kind. The text breaks off at the end of p. 26, in the sentence by which the king wills that no castellan or official …; the rest and the date stand on p. 27, which is not included.'),
 6: ('Eine Seite (S. 66) aus der Abschrift (Nr. 46 des Kopialbuchs, beginnend auf S. 63) des Dekrets eines Schiedsgerichts, durch das nach der Überschrift des Eintrags ein Stück Grund im Gut Łukom am Rand der Güter von Drzewce dem Konvent von Ląd abgetreten und abgegrenzt wurde; der Eintrag ist 1761 in der Burg Kalisch eingetragen. Die Seite zählt die Grenzhügel acht bis neunzehn mit ihren Abständen in Ruten auf, an den Wegen von Huta nach Grądzyń, nach Rosiszewo und nach Lomowo, von Drzewce und Lomowo nach Grądzyń, von Łukom nach Lomowo und von Tomice nach Zagórów und Łukom, bis zu dem Weg zu den Eckhügeln der Güter Tomice und der Stadt Pyzdry. Nachdem die Grenze des Guts Łukomia gegen Grądzyń erledigt war, ließ das Gericht auf Wunsch der Parteien zwei kleine Hügel gegen Huta öffnen, die der Konvent als Grenzhügel für sich nahm; man fand nichts darin. Am nächsten Tag, dem Freitag nach dem Sonntag Misericordia (10. April 1761), ging das Gericht zur Erneuerung der Hügel zwischen dem Gut Łukom, der Stadt Zagórów und Drzewce über, in Gegenwart des Bürgermeisters Maciej Kwiecinski, des Vogts Albert Rozewicz, des Schreibers Antoni Zalewski und anderer. Die Seite bricht in der Liste dieser Namen ab.',
     'One page (p. 66) of the copy (no. 46 of the copy-book, beginning on p. 63) of the decree of a compromissory court by which, according to the entry\'s heading, a piece of ground in the estate of Łukom by the boundary of the estate of Drzewce was ceded to the convent of Ląd and marked out; the entry was entered at Kalisz castle in 1761. The page counts the boundary mounds eight to nineteen, with their distances in rods, along the roads from Huta to Grądzyń, to Rosiszewo and to Lomowo, from Drzewce and Lomowo to Grądzyń, from Łukom to Lomowo and from Tomice to Zagórów and Łukom, up to the road to the corner mounds of the estates of Tomice and of the town of Pyzdry. When the boundary of the estate of Łukomia against Grądzyń was done, the court, at the parties\' wish, had two small hills towards Huta opened, which the convent took for itself as boundary mounds; nothing was found in them. On the next day, the Friday after Misericordia Sunday (10 April 1761), the court went on to renew the mounds between the estate of Łukom, the town of Zagórów and Drzewce, in the presence of the burgomaster Maciej Kwiecinski, the wójt Albert Rozewicz, the notary Antoni Zalewski and others. The page breaks off in the list of these names.'),
}
